From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VirusBurst <VirusBurst@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:43:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] configs: x96q_lpddr3: enable dual-rank 3/4-size DRAM (1.5
 GiB) support

Several boxes that run the X96Q image ship a 1.5 GiB LPDDR3 eMCP that is
built from two 6 Gbit dies (two ranks, 15 row / 10 column bits). The
SPL detects these as 2 GiB and U-Boot / Linux then crash or hang
("DRAM: 2 GiB (effective 0 Bytes)") as soon as the missing top quarter
of each rank is touched. Reports in the Armbian X96Q forum thread
(Mortal T1, H616 EMCP 1.5 GB boxes, X96Q "Plus" clones) match this.

CONFIG_DRAM_SUN50I_H616_SHRINK only becomes active when the SPL finds
two ranks with a nominal size of 1..2 GiB *and* the top quarter is
missing or aliases. Genuine 1 GiB and 2 GiB X96Q boards fail that test
and keep exactly the same DRAM configuration, memory map and relocation
address as before; the only cost is a few extra probe accesses in the
SPL.
---
 configs/x96q_lpddr3_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/configs/x96q_lpddr3_defconfig b/configs/x96q_lpddr3_defconfig
index 6bf4c394..4451d9c3 100644
--- a/configs/x96q_lpddr3_defconfig
+++ b/configs/x96q_lpddr3_defconfig
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR6=0x33808080
 CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR10=0x002f3359
 CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR11=0xaa889967
 CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR12=0xeeee8979
+CONFIG_DRAM_SUN50I_H616_SHRINK=y
 CONFIG_MACH_SUN50I_H616=y
 CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI_SLOT_EXTRA=2
 CONFIG_R_I2C_ENABLE=y
